[0.027, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mL\u001b[5Gok for places where concept and ideas are repeated, along with definitions, and move them to a single place which \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bis referred to with links from any areas that need to mention them.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                                                                                                    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mExamin\u001b[10G the\u001b[15Gprose for readability by a person. I want\u001b[57Git \u001b[61Go be clear, consise, direct, but also explain concepts \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bfully. Use mermaid diagrams for topics that benefit from a visual approach.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSearched for \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m files, listed \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m directories, ran \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAnswered Claude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Manifest's tasks carry an order and an ID (\"34b / W16\"). The IDs are cited in 37 code/data/script files and in \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mcommit messages. How far should renumbering go? → Order only (Recommended)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mHow \u001b[13Gine \u001b[18Ghould the per-feature\u001b[40Gtop-level\u001b[50Gdocuments be? → Major features (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· Manifest's finished stage p\u001b[36Gans (1–5, ~4,200 lines) are mostly co\u001b[74Gpleted work. Where should it go? → history/ \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfolder\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mBoth repo\u001b[18G' doc\u001b[24G change heavily. How should the work land? → Commit per repo\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ Give examples of usage when appropriate. Use the history folder idea you just posed to me for jettison as well, it's \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mhistory.md is getting large.\u001b[39m                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;193;7m\u001b[1m·\u001b[22m\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;255;193;7mScurrying… \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(1m 8s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m5.8k tokens · \u001b[38;2;255;193;7mthinking more with high effort\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Double-tap esc to rewind the code and/or conversation to a previous point in time\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;136;136;136m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── jettison-0028 ─\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[2mPress up to edit queued messages\r\u001b[38C\u001b[3B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · esc to interrupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
