[0.113, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'm\u001b[7Gplanning\u001b[16GManifest's\u001b[27Gnew\u001b[31Glayout\u001b[38Gnow\u001b[42Gthat\u001b[47Gall\u001b[51G11\u001b[54Gaudits\u001b[61Gare\u001b[65Gin.\u001b[69GFirst\u001b[75GI'm\u001b[79Gmoving\u001b[86Gthe\u001b[90Gclosed\u001b[97Gplans\u001b[103Ginto\u001b[108G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdocs/history/\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39mand splitting \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mhistory.md\u001b[39m by stage.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m1. yes\u001b[39m                                                                                                                \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m2. yes\u001b[39m                                                                                                                \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m3. Are level of detail setters needed for LODs? If so, keep them, we will add LODs later. Do some research into what \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mis\u001b[6Gn\u001b[8Geded to implement a 'nanite' (from Unreal Engine) system in this engine.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B4\u001b[9G, but quickly over 50ms\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B5\u001b[6Gyes\u001b[39m                                                                                                               \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m6.\u001b[6GIn, minimal - we will\u001b[28Glook at how needed f\u001b[49Gatsam is\u001b[58Gat a later date. for now, assume we need an editor, though it \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bis\u001b[6Gp\u001b[8Grhaps more logical for each game to ship their own and jettison to solely provide common functionality.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B7\u001b[6GAll get a backlog id.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B8\u001b[6GAdd\u001b[10Gthem to\u001b[18Gthe back\u001b[27Gog.\u001b[39m                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u0